Fix \(a\) and write \(b = b(a)\). Since \(b \leq a\), any future price that
exceeds \(a\) also exceeds \(b\). Therefore, if quote \(a\) trades within
\(L_t\) steps, then quote \(b\) also trades within \(L_t\) steps. Equivalently,
\[
    \ind{\tau_t(a) \leq L_t}
    \leq
    \ind{\tau_t(b) \leq L_t}
